WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:05.070
It was early morning when Raoul arrived at the Setting Sun Inn. Upon entering the sitting

2
00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:11.491
room, he immediately spotted Christine, who smiled at him. "I've been expecting you," she said.

3
00:00:11.492 --> 00:00:19.987
"At church this morning, I heard a voice saying you'd be here when I returned." "And

4
00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:24.757
whose voice was that?" "My poor, dead father's." There was silence while Raoul worked up the

5
00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:30.397
courage to say what was in his heart. "Did your father also say that I

6
00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:35.314
love you and cannot live without you?" Christine laughed even as she blushed. "Don't laugh, Christine.

7
00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:40.471
I'm quite serious." "I'd hoped you would come in response to my note, but I didn't

8
00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:44.236
expect you to say that. I don't know what I thought . . . perhaps

9
00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:51.133
I was wrong to write to you . . . the anniversary of my father's death

10
00:00:51.134 --> 00:01:01.544
. . . your sudden appearance in my dressing room . . ." Her voice

11
00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:10.239
trailed off again. "It all reminded me of our time together long ago." Raoul sensed that

12
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:19.034
she was under some strain. "When I came to your dressing room, was that the first

13
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:22.350
time you'd seen me at the opera house?" "No, I'd noticed you in your brother's

14
00:01:22.351 --> 00:01:26.706
box." "Then why did you pretend that you didn't know me?" he demanded. Raoul's tone was

15
00:01:26.707 --> 00:01:30.895
so hostile that Christine did not reply. "If you won't speak, I'll answer for you," Raoul

16
00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:42.384
said. "It was because there was someone else in the room, and you didn't want

17
00:01:42.385 --> 00:01:45.337
that person to know that you were interested in me." "What other person are you referring

18
00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:52.167
to?" "The man to whom you said, 'I sing only for you. I gave you my

19
00:01:53.372 --> 00:02:01.630
soul tonight, and I'm dead tired.'" Christine seized Raoul's arm and clutched it with surprising

20
00:02:01.631 --> 00:02:09.162
strength. "So you were listening outside the door?" "Yes, because I love you. I heard everything,

21
00:02:09.163 --> 00:02:15.745
including when the man asked if you loved him." At these words, Christine turned pale, and

22
00:02:15.746 --> 00:02:20.901
two tears trickled down her cheeks. Raoul tried to take her in his arms, but

23
00:02:20.902 --> 00:02:29.889
she fled in great distress. For the rest of the day, Christine remained locked in her

24
00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:36.316
room, while Raoul dejectedly roamed the snow-covered town alone. This day, which should have been

25
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:47.001
so romantic, had turned into a disaster. He was walking in the graveyard when he came

26
00:02:47.002 --> 00:02:51.246
upon red roses blooming in the snow—a surprising sign of life amid all the death around

27
00:02:51.247 --> 00:02:56.566
him. He stopped to say a prayer at Christine's father's grave. As evening fell, Raoul

28
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:04.870
wandered onto a hill overlooking the sea. He smiled as he remembered going there with Christine

29
00:03:04.871 --> 00:03:08.701
to watch for goblins dancing in the moonlight. He was startled out of his reverie by

30
00:03:08.702 --> 00:03:12.991
a voice behind him. "Do you think the goblins will come tonight?" Christine asked. Raoul

31
00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:18.815
tried to speak, but Christine put a gloved hand to his lips. "Shh, I've decided to

32
00:03:18.816 --> 00:03:27.274
tell you something serious. Do you remember the legend of the Angel of Music?" "Of course,

33
00:03:27.275 --> 00:03:32.667
and I believe it was here that your father first told us that story." "Yes,

34
00:03:32.668 --> 00:03:40.354
and it was also here that he said, 'When I am in heaven, I will send

35
00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:49.258
him to you.' Well, Raoul, my father is in heaven, and I have been visited by

36
00:03:49.259 --> 00:03:52.881
the Angel of Music." "I have no doubt about that," Raoul said. Christine appeared astonished

37
00:03:52.882 --> 00:03:58.546
at his reaction to her confession. "What do you mean?" "I mean that no one could

38
00:03:59.949 --> 00:04:07.257
sing as you did at the gala without the intervention of some higher power. No

39
00:04:07.258 --> 00:04:16.246
earthly professor of music could teach you to sing like that. You have definitely heard the

40
00:04:16.247 --> 00:04:21.562
Angel of Music, Christine." "Yes, I hear him every day in my dressing room when he

41
00:04:21.563 --> 00:04:27.820
comes to give me a lesson." "Your dressing room?" Raoul, now confused, echoed her words.

42
00:04:27.821 --> 00:04:34.360
"Yes, that's where I've heard him, and I'm not the only one. You've heard him too."

43
00:04:34.361 --> 00:04:38.915
"What? I haven't heard the Angel of Music!" "I thought I was the only one who

44
00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:46.558
could hear him, but you heard him when you were eavesdropping outside my dressing room.

45
00:04:46.559 --> 00:04:51.033
I've never seen him, but he's the one who spoke of love." Raoul burst out laughing.

46
00:04:51.034 --> 00:04:58.839
"Oh, Christine, someone is making a fool of you." With an angry cry, Christine turned and

47
00:05:00.154 --> 00:05:10.690
ran. Raoul ran after her, but she called out, "Leave me alone!" and disappeared. When

48
00:05:10.691 --> 00:05:18.257
Raoul returned to the inn, the landlady said that Christine was in her room and wouldn't

49
00:05:18.258 --> 00:05:25.505
come downstairs for dinner. Raoul dined alone and passed the rest of the long evening in

50
00:05:25.506 --> 00:05:30.279
his room, which was next to Christine's. Around half past 11, he heard her quietly

51
00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:36.974
open her door. Then she slipped downstairs, where she had a muffled conversation with the landlady.

52
00:05:36.975 --> 00:05:41.519
"Don't lose the key!" the landlady cautioned her. Raoul waited until Christine had left the

53
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.946
inn and locked the door to his room. He didn't want to face the landlady, so

54
00:05:46.947 --> 00:05:52.424
he climbed out his window and down a tree. Following Christine to the graveyard, he made

55
00:05:52.425 --> 00:05:58.838
no attempt to walk quietly on the hard snow. But she never turned around, and

56
00:06:00.248 --> 00:06:07.360
soon reached her father's grave, where she knelt in prayer. At that moment the church clock

57
00:06:07.361 --> 00:06:14.370
struck midnight, and Raoul suddenly heard violin music. It was one of the tunes that Christine's

58
00:06:14.371 --> 00:06:19.816
father used to play for them as children. "If Christine's angel exists, he couldn't play

59
00:06:19.817 --> 00:06:26.775
more beautifully," Raoul said to himself. He was not the only one affected by the music;

60
00:06:26.776 --> 00:06:36.440
Christine stretched out her arms with joy, and her face radiated happiness. Suddenly the music stopped,

61
00:06:36.441 --> 00:06:43.599
and Raoul saw a shadow gliding along the wall of the church. Raoul glanced at

62
00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:49.769
Christine, but she was still lost in thought at her father's grave. The shadow had already

63
00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:56.693
entered the dark church, but Raoul was quick enough to grab a corner of its cloak.

64
00:06:58.032 --> 00:07:05.403
At that moment they reached the altar, and moonbeams fell straight on them through the

65
00:07:05.404 --> 00:07:10.692
stained glass window. The figure turned around, and Raoul saw a terrible skull with glowing eyes.

66
00:07:10.693 --> 00:07:19.189
He fell to the ground and remembered nothing until he regained consciousness at the inn

67
00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:28.941
later that morning. "Where am I? What happened?" Raoul said. Christine leaned over his bed, and

68
00:07:28.942 --> 00:07:37.192
the landlady hovered in the background. "Oh, Raoul, you gave us such an awful fright!" Christine

69
00:07:37.193 --> 00:07:45.008
warmed his fingers between her hands. "The church sexton found you stretched out in front

70
00:07:45.009 --> 00:07:48.883
of the altar and brought you back here half-frozen. I thought you were going to die!"

